      hack_0_cat: "Savings & Water",
      hack_0_title: "Nasoni: Free chilled drinking water all over Rome",
      hack_0_detail: "Don't buy €3 water bottles near monuments. Bring a reusable bottle and refill it at any of the 2,500 iron street fountains (\"Nasoni\"): the water flows straight from mountain aqueducts.",
      hack_1_cat: "Free Viewpoint",
      hack_1_title: "45th Floor Observatory at Tokyo Metropolitan Gov't Building (Shinjuku)",
      hack_1_detail: "While other observation decks cost $25-$30 USD, the Shinjuku Government towers offer 100% free entry, 360° panoramic views (including Mt. Fuji on clear days), and an evening light show.",
      hack_2_cat: "Views & Access",
      hack_2_title: "Free panoramic rooftop terrace at Galeries Lafayette Haussmann",
      hack_2_detail: "Head up to the top floor (7th floor) of Galeries Lafayette Haussmann for one of the best open views of the Palais Garnier and Eiffel Tower completely free with no queue.",
      hack_3_cat: "Transport",
      hack_3_title: "Staten Island Ferry + OMNY weekly fare cap on the NYC Subway",
      hack_3_detail: "See the Statue of Liberty and Manhattan skyline at sunset for free on the Staten Island Ferry from Whitehall Terminal. Plus, tapping the same contactless card (OMNY) makes rides free after 12 trips in a week.",
      hack_4_cat: "Free Museums",
      hack_4_title: "Free entry hours at Museo del Prado & Reina Sofía",
      hack_4_detail: "Madrid's Prado Museum is free Mon–Sat 18:00–20:00 (Sun 17:00–19:00), and Reina Sofía (home to Picasso's Guernica) is free Mon and Wed–Sat 19:00–21:00. Book the free slot online.",
      hack_5_cat: "Tickets",
      hack_5_title: "Sagrada Familia light hours & Sant Pau Art Nouveau Site",
      hack_5_detail: "Book Sagrada Familia around 09:00 AM or 16:30 PM to see sunlight stream through the stained glass. Just 10 minutes down Av. Gaudí sits Recinto Modernista de Sant Pau, an architectural gem with far fewer crowds.",
      hack_0_city: "Rome", hack_1_city: "Tokyo", hack_2_city: "Paris", hack_3_city: "New York", hack_4_city: "Madrid", hack_5_city: "Barcelona",
      hilo_1_dest: "Rome", hilo_1_level: "Explorer Level 4 · 6 trips", hilo_1_date: "2 hours ago",
      hilo_1_title: "Real guide to booking the Colosseum & Vatican without reseller markups",
      hilo_1_body: "Just got back from 5 days in Rome planned with Plux. For the Colosseum (Arena access), book exactly 30 days ahead at 08:45 AM (Italy time) on the official Parco Archeologico site. It costs €18-€24 vs €75 from third-party agencies. For the Vatican Museums, the 08:00 AM slot lets you reach the Sistine Chapel almost empty.",
      hilo_1_itinerary: "Imperial Rome & Vatican (3 Days · 9 activities)",
      hilo_1_r0_date: "1 hour ago", hilo_1_r0_text: "Totally agree. One key tip: on Rome's public transit (bus & metro) you no longer need paper tickets—just tap your contactless card or phone with Tap & Go (€1.50 per 100 minutes).",
      hilo_1_r1_date: "35 min ago", hilo_1_r1_text: "Awesome tip on the 08:00 AM Vatican slot, I just cloned your template into my account.",
      hilo_2_dest: "Tokyo", hilo_2_level: "Nomad Level 5 · 9 trips", hilo_2_date: "5 hours ago",
      hilo_2_title: "Is the JR Pass worth it in Japan now or are single Shinkansen tickets better?",
      hilo_2_body: "After the nationwide Japan Rail Pass price hike, we ran the numbers in Plux's multi-currency budget for the classic Tokyo - Kyoto - Osaka - Tokyo loop (12 days). Buying individual Nozomi Shinkansen tickets via SmartEX saved us nearly 32% compared to a 7-day JR Pass.",
      hilo_2_itinerary: "Traditional & Futuristic Tokyo (3 Days · 9 activities)",
      hilo_2_r0_date: "3 hours ago", hilo_2_r0_text: "Exactly, for the Golden Route (Tokyo-Kyoto-Osaka) single tickets + a Suica card in Apple Wallet are better today. The regional pass that still delivers huge value is the JR Kansai-Hiroshima Area Pass.",
      hilo_3_dest: "Mendoza", hilo_3_level: "Pro Traveler Level 4 · 5 trips", hilo_3_date: "Yesterday",
      hilo_3_title: "Our winery route in Luján de Cuyo & Uco Valley + High Andes",
      hilo_3_body: "Sharing our Mendoza route for anyone visiting this month. We booked Catena Zapata and a tasting lunch 3 weeks ahead. If you import booking emails in the Import Bookings tab, times and split costs fill in automatically.",
      hilo_3_itinerary: "Wine & Mountains Route in Mendoza (Community)",
      hilo_3_r0_date: "Yesterday", hilo_3_r0_text: "Already cloned the template! Do you recommend renting a car or hiring a driver between wineries?",
      hilo_4_dest: "Barcelona", hilo_4_level: "Explorer Level 3 · 3 trips", hilo_4_date: "2 days ago",
      hilo_4_title: "Group trip across Spain & Italy in November: looking for tips and splitting costs",
      hilo_4_body: "Four friends planning Barcelona -> Paris -> Rome. We're using Plux's collaborative link and entering each booking in its original currency (EUR & USD). Sharing our Barcelona base in case anyone overlaps dates.",
      hilo_4_itinerary: "Modernist & Mediterranean Barcelona (3 Days)",
      hilo_4_r0_date: "1 day ago", hilo_4_r0_text: "To travel from Barcelona to Paris, check the direct TGV Inoui train from Barcelona Sants to Paris Gare de Lyon—it saves the 2-hour airport wait."
